OK.  After taking a closer look, it's not just if you try to cancel; it
_is_ if you hit any random non-directional key.  This is silly, and is
now fixed for all direction prompts that happen to use that code -- the
user needs to either explicitly cancel, or at least pick SOME sort of valid
direction before it'll let him out.  Note that spacebar _is_ listed in
quitchars as a cancel key (along with \r, \n, and ESC), though.

If you try to cancel, it will still lob the spell in a random
direction.  Without being a mind reader, I suspect that this is because
the chance of casting success has already been rolled, confirmed, and 
the Pw deducted from the player; I suspect the original coder opted to 
simply "release the magical energy" rather than try to rewind beyond 
a certain point.

